Finite-strain U3 force (stage 1 of the NLGEOM port).

Under NLGEOM the U3 element returns the Hencky-elastic force of
eqs. (1)-(17) through the new kernel u3nl.f, which shares its geometry and
its weight walk with u3vol.f.  U2 returns NO separate force in that mode:
the finite-strain force evaluates the full Hencky stress of Fbar and pairs
it with the ES-FEM motion, so its linearisation IS U2 + U3 -- adding the
small-strain deviatoric force on top of it would count the deviatoric half
twice.  The stiffness split is untouched and remains the iteration matrix.

The force is validated inside ccx against the prototype: on a NLGEOM
boundary-value problem the reactions at the prescribed boundary equal
FbarNL.force(u_ccx) to 1.4e-7 (elements_ccx/tests/verify_nlccx.py), and the
finite-strain branch is measurably active (5.6e-2 away from the linear
force).  The consistent tangent is stage 2; until it lands the modified
Newton converges only at small strain.

  Makefile.inc        builds u3nl.f
  resultsmech_u.f     passes iperturb to the U2/U3 dispatchers

The element sources themselves (u3nl.f, resultsmech_u2.f, resultsmech_u3.f)
live in ../elements_ccx/ and are copied into src/ before building; add
u3nl.f to SCCXF as this patch does.

--- resultsmech_u.f
+++ resultsmech_u.f
@@ -73,13 +73,13 @@
 !     F-barES-FEM-T4: U3 F-barES-FEM-T4 volumetric edge domain
 !
          call resultsmech_u3(co,kon,ipkon,lakon,ne,v,elcon,nelcon,
-     &        ielmat,mi,ncmat_,ntmat_,fn,calcul_fn,nal,nelem)
+     &        ielmat,mi,ncmat_,ntmat_,fn,calcul_fn,nal,nelem,iperturb)
       elseif(lakon(nelem)(2:2).eq.'2') then
 !
 !     F-barES-FEM-T4: U2 F-barES-FEM-T4 deviatoric edge domain
 !
          call resultsmech_u2(co,kon,ipkon,lakon,ne,v,elcon,nelcon,
-     &        ielmat,mi,ncmat_,ntmat_,fn,calcul_fn,nal,nelem)
+     &        ielmat,mi,ncmat_,ntmat_,fn,calcul_fn,nal,nelem,iperturb)
       elseif(lakon(nelem)(2:2).eq.'4') then
 !
 !     F-barES-FEM-T4: U4 null base tetrahedron of the F-barES-FEM-T4 element
--- Makefile.inc
+++ Makefile.inc
@@ -279,6 +279,7 @@
 	e_c3d_u3.f \
 	u2edge.f \
 	u3vol.f \
+	u3nl.f \
 	resultsmech_u2.f \
 	resultsmech_u3.f \
